 "text": "[energetic] In 2019, a top-performing analyst named Maya got escorted out of her building by security. [knowing] The whole disaster started because she held the office door for two seconds. [upbeat] It was a pouring Monday morning. Maya tapped her keycard, and a sharp-dressed guy juggling two hot coffees sprinted up behind her yelling, \"Hold on, thanks!\" [amused] Being polite, Maya flashed a smile and held the office door. [suspicious] Only problem? He didn't work there—not even close. While Maya waited for the elevator, [fast-paced] he strolled past three cubicles and slid an unlocked laptop into his leather bag. [deadpan] He even waved at the front desk walking out. Nobody glanced up. [dramatic] Turns out that single laptop held private financial records for two hundred major clients. Before dinner, every file was up for auction [fast-paced] online—and fraud investigators were tearing the entire office apart. [serious] Security pulled one ten-second lobby clip, [serious] and Maya's career vanished before Friday. No second chance, no severance—just a cardboard box. [deadpan] She'd literally just held the office door. [ironic] Even today, every single new hire watches her ten-second clip on orientation morning.",
